GitLab setup (Mac) — clone repo
put into gpt and it will help
1) Create a Personal Access Token (PAT)

Open GitLab in browser (campus GitLab)

Go to User Settings → Personal access tokens

Create token with scopes:

✅ read_repository

✅ write_repository

Copy the token somewhere safe (don’t share it)

Don’t tick everything. Don’t post the token in chats.

2) Clear any old saved credentials (Keychain)

Open Terminal and run:

printf "protocol=https\nhost=campus.cs.le.ac.uk\n" | git credential-osxkeychain erase
printf "protocol=https\nhost=hi69@campus.cs.le.ac.uk\n" | git credential-osxkeychain erase


(Optional but useful)

git config --global credential.helper osxkeychain

3) Clone the repo into your folder

Go to where you keep projects (example: ~/Intelji):

cd ~/Intelji
git clone https://campus.cs.le.ac.uk/gitlab/co2303_2026/Group-76.git


When prompted:

Username: your GitLab username (or full uni email)

Password: paste the token (PAT), not your normal password

4) Checkout the correct branch (if needed)
cd Group-76
git branch -a
git checkout Project_main


If Project_main isn’t local:

git checkout -b Project_main origin/Project_main

5) Add your code, commit, push

Copy your Spring Boot project files into the repo folder, then:

git add .
git commit -m "Add Spring Boot starter project"
git push -u origin Project_main

Common issues
“HTTP Basic: Access denied”

You used your normal password instead of the token, OR

Keychain has an old password/token saved → do step 2 again.

Token leaked

Revoke it immediately in GitLab and create a new one.

